==== Modifications (Edge API / RandallFlare) ====

This tree is a modified version of QuantumNous/new-api, rewritten to run as a
Cloudflare Workers-compatible Worker on RandallFlare (workerd + D1 + KV +
static assets via @bigrandall/rrangler).

Material changes from upstream:

- Runtime: Go/Gin + embedded React replaced by a TypeScript Worker on workerd.
- Storage: MySQL/PostgreSQL/SQLite-via-GORM replaced by D1 (SQLite) + KV.
- Password hashing: Argon2id/bcrypt replaced by Web Crypto PBKDF2-SHA256
  (existing upstream password hashes are not portable). This is documented
  PBKDF2-SHA256, not a fake Argon2 implementation.
- Dashboard access tokens are original-shaped JWTs (HS256, iss=new-api,
  aud=new-api-dashboard, 15-minute TTL). The HttpOnly refresh cookie
  `new_api_refresh` is the original `sid.secret` value (Path=/api/user/auth,
  SameSite=Strict) with rotation and AUTH_REFRESH_RACE. Security proofs are
  original-shaped JWTs (`token_use=security_proof`, 1-minute TTL) sent as
  `X-Security-Proof` and consumed once via hashed auth_flows rows.
- The original QuantumNous/new-api TanStack + Rsbuild frontend is vendored
  under web/ and served as ASSETS (public/ is the production build). It is
  not a compact replacement SPA.
- Channel types that require vendor SDKs or local plugins (in-process JS task
  plugins) are exposed in the catalog and will relay when the channel is
  OpenAI/Anthropic/Gemini compatible or uses HTTP pass-through; otherwise they
  return a structured error. Vertex ADC uses the original HTTP path (RS256 JWT
  + `https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v4/token`, no Google SDK). AWS AKSK uses
  the original HTTP path (Bedrock `InvokeModel` / `InvokeModelWithResponseStream`
  + SigV4 service `bedrock`, no AWS SDK). AWS ConvertClaudeRequest rewrites
  `source.type=url` to base64 via original GetBase64Data JSON (`type`, `media_type`,
  `data`, omit empty `url`). Extra-OK: skip gin file-source context cache, Worker
  download proxy, ValidateSSRFProtectedFetchURL, and HEIF `decodeImageConfig`.
  OpenAI chat/Responses ConvertRequest HTTP image, file, input_audio, and
  video_url sources are rewritten to Claude `source.type=base64` /
  Gemini `inlineData` via original `MediaContent.ToFileSource` + GetBase64Data
  (`get file data failed: …` / `get file data from '…' failed: …`). Extra-OK:
  ConvertOpenAIRequest stays sync; URL fetch runs in convertOutbound before
  ConvertRequest. xAI ConvertOpenAIResponsesRequest fills empty `model` from
  UpstreamModelName and does not run openai.Adaptor reasoning-suffix stripping.
  Volcengine TTS uses the original HTTP path
  (`wss://openspeech.bytedance.com/api/v1/tts/ws_binary` binary frames, or
  `{base}/v1/audio/speech` JSON `code` 3000, no Volc SDK). Xunfei SparkDesk uses the original HTTP path
  (gorilla `Dial` handshake timeout 5s, HTTP 101 `Upgrade: websocket` to
  `wss://spark-api.xf-yun.com/{version}/chat`, no gorilla SDK). OpenAI Realtime uses the original HTTP path
  (gorilla `DefaultDialer` 45s, HTTP 101 `Upgrade: websocket`, `https`→`wss`, Azure
  `/openai/realtime?deployment=` + `api-key`, preview-only `openai-beta`, Advanced Custom
  route `https`→`wss` + route auth, OpenaiRealtimeHandler `RealtimeUsage` JSON +
  CountTokenRealtime / PreWssConsumeQuota / PostWssConsumeQuota, no gorilla SDK).
  Cloudflare Workers AI STT uses the original HTTP path (`ConvertAudioRequest` raw
  `file` bytes, GetRequestURL `/client/v4/accounts/{ApiVersion}/ai/run/{model}`,
  cfSTTHandler `{text}` from `{result.text}`, ResponseText2Usage completion tokens).
  Extra-OK: STT prompt tokens skip original `GetAudioDuration`.
  OpenAI-model realtime text tokens use original `EstimateToken` (tiktoken-go is not
  bundled). Dial-first 101 then async usage is extra-OK vs original upgrade-first
  then blocking handler. Stripe/Epay/Creem/Waffo checkout use HTTP APIs
  (no vendor SDK). io.net model deployments use the original HTTP API (no
  vendor SDK). Original QuantumNous factory task plugins (`plugins/tasks/*/plugin.js`)
  are embedded and listed/routed with original JSON (`source: "factory"`).
  Task-plugin `plugin.js` hooks run through the original jsplugin contract
  (forbidden syntax, host `utils`, Call/CallMember, HookError, dry-run JSON)
  on workerd. This is not Goja/sobek; tight-loop Interrupt is the isolate CPU
  limit.   Native plugin routes run original `PrepareTaskPluginRoute`
  (`native.decode` / `native.render` / `native.error` JSON) before submit
  channel distribution. Native submit uses original RelayTask
  `buildSubmitRequest` / `parseSubmitResponse` / `native.render` JSON
  (public `task_id`, no `clientResponse`, `X-New-Api-Other-Ratios`).
  Native query uses original `buildQueryRequest` / `parseTaskResult` /
  `updateVideoSingleTask` JSON (`queryContext` without `requestBody`, public
  `task_id` in `native.render`, persisted `result_url` / `plugin_state`).
  `/v1/videos/:task_id` retrieve uses original `ConvertToOpenAIVideo`
  (`protocols.openai_video.render` + host-owned id/status/progress/model).
- Passkey RP IDs use original `idna.Lookup.ToASCII` then
  `publicsuffix.EffectiveTLDPlusOne` / `PublicSuffix` (golang.org/x/net
  v0.55.0 algorithm + PSL git d6c92f1). Passwords remain documented
  PBKDF2-SHA256, not a fake Argon2 implementation.

